data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** It works just like any other unmanaged type:

```csharp
Span<nint> span = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> uspan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

The only caveat: `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context because the size isn't fixed at compile time (it's 8 bytes on 64-bit, 4 on 32-bit). But the `stackalloc` itself works in a safe context when assigned to a `Span<T>`.
